1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,450
There's a setting on your phone you've never seen.

2
00:00:04,580 --> 00:00:09,107
It only shows up at 3:33 AM.

3
00:00:09,237 --> 00:00:12,001
It's called... Hidden Mode.

4
00:00:12,131 --> 00:00:16,770
And no matter what happens... never turn it on.

5
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:19,861
You turned it on.

6
00:00:19,991 --> 00:00:24,890
At first, nothing happens. No sound. No pop-up.

7
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:28,736
Just a tiny blue dot, right next to your battery.

8
00:00:28,866 --> 00:00:31,080
So you go back to sleep.

9
00:00:31,710 --> 00:00:35,508
In the morning, you have one new notification.

10
00:00:35,638 --> 00:00:37,639
It's from your best friend, Jake.

11
00:00:37,769 --> 00:00:43,524
It says: "Bro... I can't believe you fell in the cafeteria."

12
00:00:43,654 --> 00:00:50,304
Which is weird. Because it's 7 AM. And you haven't even left for school.

13
00:00:50,434 --> 00:00:53,986
Then you see the time on the message.

14
00:00:54,116 --> 00:00:57,033
12:41 PM. Today.

15
00:00:57,163 --> 00:01:02,336
The message... hasn't been sent yet.

16
00:01:02,916 --> 00:01:08,979
At 12:40, you walk into the cafeteria. Very... slowly.

17
00:01:09,109 --> 00:01:15,288
And there it is. A puddle of spilled milk. Right where you would have stepped.

18
00:01:15,418 --> 00:01:17,323
You step over it.

19
00:01:17,623 --> 00:01:21,273
JAKE: Bro... why are you walking like a ninja?

20
00:01:21,703 --> 00:01:25,668
12:41. Jake doesn't send anything. Because nothing happened.

21
00:01:25,798 --> 00:01:32,728
You check your phone. The notification is gone. Like it never existed.

22
00:01:32,858 --> 00:01:36,539
And your battery? 99%.

23
00:01:36,669 --> 00:01:43,965
Hidden Mode doesn't show you the future. It shows you notifications from the future.

24
00:01:44,095 --> 00:01:47,077
And you just deleted one.

25
00:01:47,657 --> 00:01:50,414
So, you start using it.

26
00:01:50,544 --> 00:01:55,527
A text from your teacher: "Pop quiz tomorrow. Chapter 7."

27
00:01:55,657 --> 00:02:02,654
You read Chapter 7. You get an A. Your teacher looks... suspicious.

28
00:02:02,954 --> 00:02:07,376
MR. HALL: An A. From you. Hm.

29
00:02:07,806 --> 00:02:11,911
A weather alert: "Heavy rain at 4:15."

30
00:02:12,041 --> 00:02:16,698
You bring an umbrella. Everyone else gets soaked.

31
00:02:16,998 --> 00:02:19,496
JAKE: How did you know it was gonna rain?!

32
00:02:19,926 --> 00:02:24,163
A message from your bank: "Your card was declined."

33
00:02:24,293 --> 00:02:26,169
You don't buy the sneakers.

34
00:02:26,299 --> 00:02:31,678
For one whole week, you are the luckiest person alive.

35
00:02:31,808 --> 00:02:36,957
40 notifications changed. 40 little disasters... gone.

36
00:02:37,587 --> 00:02:39,430
Then you notice your battery.

37
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:42,975
60%. And it's plugged in.

38
00:02:43,105 --> 00:02:47,362
It doesn't charge anymore. It only goes down.

39
00:02:47,492 --> 00:02:52,774
1%... every time you change the future.

40
00:02:52,904 --> 00:02:57,452
Fine. You'll just turn it off.

41
00:02:57,582 --> 00:03:01,488
Except... the toggle is gone.

42
00:03:01,618 --> 00:03:09,262
You restart the phone. You reset it. You even buy a new one.

43
00:03:09,392 --> 00:03:13,593
The blue dot shows up on every phone you touch.

44
00:03:13,723 --> 00:03:20,113
And the notifications keep coming. And you keep fixing them. Because how could you not?

45
00:03:20,243 --> 00:03:23,371
20%. 10%. 5%.

46
00:03:23,501 --> 00:03:24,982
3%.

47
00:03:25,712 --> 00:03:27,835
That's when they change.

48
00:03:27,965 --> 00:03:34,712
They stop coming from your friends. They start coming from... you.

49
00:03:34,842 --> 00:03:36,382
"Stop changing things."

50
00:03:36,512 --> 00:03:38,686
"You don't know what you're using up."

51
00:03:38,816 --> 00:03:43,351
"Save the rest. You're going to need it."

52
00:03:43,481 --> 00:03:45,270
So you stop.

53
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:51,306
You let everything happen. You trip in the cafeteria. You fail a quiz. You get soaked.

54
00:03:51,436 --> 00:03:55,307
And your battery holds. 3%.

55
00:03:56,237 --> 00:04:03,390
Then, at 3:33 AM... one last notification.

56
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:05,844
It's from your mom.

57
00:04:05,974 --> 00:04:15,276
Sent tomorrow. 8:14 AM. "Running late. Taking the highway. Love you."

58
00:04:15,406 --> 00:04:21,962
That's all it says. But the screen around it... is shaking.

59
00:04:22,092 --> 00:04:26,284
And suddenly, the messages from yourself make sense.

60
00:04:26,414 --> 00:04:33,197
You weren't telling yourself to stop. You were saving the battery. For this.

61
00:04:33,727 --> 00:04:37,361
In the morning, you hide her car keys.

62
00:04:37,661 --> 00:04:40,611
MOM: Where are my keys?! I'm gonna be so late!

63
00:04:41,041 --> 00:04:45,434
She's late. She's furious. She takes the long way.

64
00:04:45,564 --> 00:04:55,706
At 8:14, there's a huge crash on the highway. Your mom is 20 miles away, stuck behind a school bus, still yelling at you on the phone.

65
00:04:55,836 --> 00:05:00,993
Battery: 1%. It cost you 2.

66
00:05:01,123 --> 00:05:08,531
That night, your mom hugs you a little longer than usual. She doesn't know why.

67
00:05:08,831 --> 00:05:09,986
MOM: Love you, kiddo.

68
00:05:11,017 --> 00:05:16,947
Then your phone lights up. A pop-up you've never seen before.

69
00:05:17,077 --> 00:05:23,321
"Hidden Mode update available. Install tonight at 3:33 AM?"

70
00:05:23,451 --> 00:05:29,992
And under it... one more message. From you. Sent tomorrow.

71
00:05:30,622 --> 00:05:34,316
"Whatever you do... don't install it."
